<body>

<header class="report-header">
  <div class="tag">Analytics Report &mdash; Chess</div>
  <h1>Lichess Chess Game Analytics:<br>Patterns of Victory, Openings, and Player Dynamics</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">A comprehensive data-driven analysis of 20,058 Lichess games examining color advantage, rating dynamics, opening effectiveness, and time control patterns.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <div class="meta-item"><strong>Dataset:</strong> Lichess.org via Kaggle (datasnaek/chess)</div>
    <div class="meta-item"><strong>Games Analyzed:</strong> 20,058</div>
    <div class="meta-item"><strong>Audience:</strong> Analysts &amp; Coaches</div>
    <div class="meta-item"><strong>Report Date:</strong> April 2026</div>
  </div>
</header>

<main class="content">

  <!-- KPI Bar -->
  <div class="kpi-bar">
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="label">Total Games</div>
      <div class="value">20,058</div>
      <div class="sub">80.5% rated</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="label">White Win Rate</div>
      <div class="value">52.3%</div>
      <div class="sub">of decisive games</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="label">Avg. Game Length</div>
      <div class="value">60.5</div>
      <div class="sub">half-moves (plies)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="label">Checkmate Rate</div>
      <div class="value">31.5%</div>
      <div class="sub">of all games</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="label">Draw Rate</div>
      <div class="value">4.7%</div>
      <div class="sub">950 drawn games</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="label">Rating Range</div>
      <div class="value">784–2723</div>
      <div class="sub">Elo (both colors)</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 1: OVERVIEW -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-num">1</div>
      <h2>Dataset Overview &amp; Game Distribution</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p>The dataset comprises <strong>20,058 completed Lichess games</strong> collected via the Lichess API, with each row representing a unique rated or casual game. A strong majority&mdash;<strong>16,155 games (80.5%)</strong>&mdash;were rated, meaning outcomes affected Elo ratings. The remaining 3,903 (19.5%) were casual.</p>

