      <p>The first-move advantage is a foundational concept in competitive chess. Across the full dataset, <strong>white won 10,001 games (49.9% of all games) versus black's 9,107 (45.4%)</strong>. Excluding the 950 draws, white wins <strong>52.3% of decisive games</strong> and black wins <strong>47.7%</strong>&mdash;a 4.6 percentage-point edge for white.</p>

