          <div class="chart-container" style="height:260px">
            <canvas id="diffChart"></canvas>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="insight">
        <strong>Rating differentials are the single strongest predictor of outcomes.</strong> When two players are within 50 Elo of each other, the nominally higher-rated player wins only <strong>48.9%</strong>&mdash;essentially a coin flip. At a 200-point gap the favorite wins <strong>64%</strong>, at 300–500 points the figure rises to <strong>79.2%</strong>, and beyond 500 points it reaches <strong>84.9%</strong>. This near-linear progression confirms Elo's predictive validity at scale.
