      <p style="margin-top:14px;"><strong>Draw rates rise with time:</strong> Rapid/Classical has a <strong>6.6% draw rate</strong>—more than double the Blitz draw rate of ~4.0%. This mirrors the pattern seen at professional levels, where more time allows both players to navigate to balanced endgames rather than blundering into decisive errors.</p>

      <p>Average game length peaks in Blitz (6–10 min) at <strong>62.3 turns</strong>, then somewhat paradoxically dips in longer formats. This may reflect faster resignations in classical formats once a material disadvantage becomes clear, compared to blitz where players often play on hoping the opponent flags.</p>
