          <div class="finding-body">White wins <strong>52.3% of decisive games</strong> overall, a consistent 4.6pp edge. However, this advantage is concentrated in the 1,200–1,800 Elo range (53–54%). At 2,000+ Elo the gap narrows to just <strong>50.6%</strong>—within statistical noise for the sample size. This confirms that opening preparation, which neutralizes white's initiative, is a key skill separator at higher ratings. Platform design interventions (e.g., opening training tools) targeting players in the 1,400–1,800 range would have the most measurable impact on evening color-based outcomes.</div>
