          <div class="finding-title">Rating Differential is the Dominant Outcome Predictor</div>
          <div class="finding-body">The higher-rated player's win probability scales almost linearly from <strong>48.9%</strong> (0–50 point gap) to <strong>84.9%</strong> (500+ point gap). A 200-point gap already confers a <strong>64% win probability</strong>. This validates Elo as a strong predictor in this dataset and confirms that matchmaking quality—not opening choice—drives most outcome variance. For coaches: players at a significant rating disadvantage should focus on time-management and practical fighting chances rather than theoretical preparation.</div>
        </div>
